---
import ResponsiveImage from './solutions/ResponsiveImage.astro';
import WarehouseOpsCloud from './WarehouseOpsCloud.astro';
import WarehouseOpsFaq from './WarehouseOpsFaq.astro';
import WarehouseEnquiry from './WarehouseOpsEnquiry.astro';
import '../styles/warehouse-ops.css';
const risks=[
 {n:'01',title:'Floor & installation',body:'Floor settlement, uneven support or an initial alignment deviation can change the rack’s installed geometry.'},
 {n:'02',title:'Handling & impact',body:'Forklift contact and repeated loading can leave damage or residual movement that needs a closer inspection.'},
 {n:'03',title:'Connections & protection',body:'Loose fixings, missing beam locks and damaged or absent guards remain physical inspection priorities.'},
 {n:'04',title:'Loads & deferred repairs',body:'Changed loading, incompatible replacement parts or unrepaired damage require review by a competent rack specialist.'}
];
const scenes=[
 {image:'warehouse-hero',n:'01',title:'Pallet racking & distribution',text:'Frequent loading. Shared aisles. Prioritise selected uprights and keep each event tied to its bay.',tag:'Rack tilt · Handling context'},
 {image:'warehouse-asrs',n:'02',title:'High-bay & automated storage',text:'Plan accessible monitoring points and controlled installation windows around the automated equipment.',tag:'Rack tilt · Access planning'},
 {image:'cold-storage',n:'03',title:'Cold stores & food logistics',text:'Separate structural inspection from stock-condition monitoring. Select temperature and humidity sensing for the storage duty.',tag:'Rack tilt · Temperature · Humidity'},
 {image:'warehouse-ehs',n:'04',title:'Work areas & personnel exposure',text:'Use the identified bay to organise access control, traffic diversion and a responsible site check.',tag:'Location · Site control · EHS response'}
];
const crops={rack:'--crop-aspect:635/811;--crop-width:198.425197%;--crop-left:-14.015748%;--crop-top:-55.240444%;',device:'--crop-aspect:414/327;--crop-width:304.347826%;--crop-left:-182.608696%;--crop-top:-137.920489%;',people:'--crop-aspect:414/424;--crop-width:304.347826%;--crop-left:-182.608696%;--crop-top:-196.933962%;'};
---
<div class="scope-v2 warehouse-v7 warehouse-ops">
  <section class="ops-hero" id="wh-overview" data-module="01" aria-labelledby="warehouse-title">
    <div class="ops-wrap">
      <nav class="ops-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="https://www.hitelecom.com/solution">Solutions</a><span>/</span><span>Smart warehousing</span></nav>
      <div class="ops-hero-grid">
        <div class="ops-hero-copy"><p class="ops-eyebrow">RACK TILT MONITORING / OPERATIONS & EHS</p>
          <h1 id="warehouse-title">Warehouse rack<br/>tilt monitoring.<br/><em>Know where to act.</em></h1>
          <p class="ops-hero-lead">Record angle changes between inspections. Identify the upright, notify the responsible team and give the next site check a clear starting point.</p>
          <div class="ops-actions"><a class="ops-button" href="#enquiry">Discuss your warehouse <span>↗</span></a><a class="ops-text-link" href="#wh-monitoring">Why add tilt monitoring? <span>↓</span></a></div>
          <p class="ops-hero-note">For warehouse supervisors, EHS leaders and rack maintenance teams.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="ops-hero-image"><ResponsiveImage imageKey="warehouse-hero" alt="Warehouse application illustration showing pallet racks and clearly defined storage aisles" priority={true} sizes="(max-width:800px) calc(100vw - 40px), 550px"/><div class="ops-image-label"><span>EVERY MEASUREMENT HAS A LOCATION</span><strong>Warehouse. Row. Bay. Upright.</strong></div><figcaption>Application illustration</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
      <div class="ops-outcomes"><a href="#wh-monitoring"><span>01 / VISIBILITY</span><strong>Changes between inspections</strong><i>↗</i></a><a href="#wh-signals"><span>02 / FOCUS</span><strong>Changes that need review</strong><i>↗</i></a><a href="#wh-cloud"><span>03 / OWNERSHIP</span><strong>A named person to respond</strong><i>↗</i></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <nav class="ops-local-nav" aria-label="Warehouse solution sections"><div class="ops-wrap"><a href="#wh-monitoring">Why monitor</a><a href="#wh-signals">Sensor & signals</a><a href="#wh-cloud">Cloud & response</a><a href="#wh-applications">Applications</a><a href="#wh-hardware">Installation</a><a href="#wh-evidence">EHS & records</a></div></nav>

  <section class="ops-section" id="wh-monitoring" data-module="02" aria-labelledby="monitoring-title"><div class="ops-wrap">
    <div class="ops-heading"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">02 / WHY ADD TILT MONITORING?</p><h2 id="monitoring-title">What changed since<br/>the last inspection?</h2></div><p>Racks stay in service between checks. Angle history adds a record of change at selected uprights, so teams know where to look next.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-compare">
      <article class="ops-compare-manual"><div class="ops-compare-top"><span>EXISTING INSPECTION PROGRAMME</span><span class="ops-ring">01</span></div><h3>Condition observed<br/>at the visit.</h3><p>People check loading, guards, fixings and visible damage. Findings depend on what is observed and reported.</p><div class="ops-visit-timeline" aria-label="Scheduled inspection, an interval without automated angle records, next inspection"><b>Inspection</b><span>Between visits</span><b>Inspection</b></div><div class="ops-compare-result">No automatic angle history at the point.</div></article>
      <article class="ops-compare-sensor"><div class="ops-compare-top"><span>INSPECTIONS + TILT MONITORING</span><span class="ops-ring">02</span></div><h3>Changes recorded<br/>between visits.</h3><p>Selected upright angles are measured against a baseline. Configured events identify the point for review.</p><div class="ops-signal-timeline" aria-label="Illustrative sequence of regular measurements with an angle change identified"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="ops-event"></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Point identified ↗</b></div><div class="ops-compare-result">Angle + location + time for the next site check.</div></article>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-risk-intro"><h3>What can put a rack at risk?</h3><p>Angle data is one part of the inspection picture.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-risks">{risks.map(r=><article><span>{r.n}</span><h4>{r.title}</h4><p>{r.body}</p></article>)}</div>
    <p class="ops-note ops-boundary">A tilt sensor measures local orientation. It does not directly measure settlement, load capacity or every damaged component. The absence of an alert does not establish rack safety.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ops-section ops-pale" id="wh-signals" data-module="03" aria-labelledby="signals-title"><div class="ops-wrap">
    <div class="ops-heading"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">03 / THE SENSOR & THE SIGNAL</p><h2 id="signals-title">See the movement.<br/>Understand the context.</h2></div><p>Normal loading rebound, sustained angle change and short impacts need different interpretation and response.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-product"><figure><img src="/assets/solutions/ops-tilt-product.png" width="929" height="1016" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Hitelecom wireless tilt sensor, silver enclosure with antenna"/><figcaption>Product reference · Supplied configuration may vary</figcaption></figure><div class="ops-product-copy"><p class="ops-eyebrow">WIRELESS RACK TILT SENSOR</p><h3>Local angle.<br/>A reliable reference.</h3><p>Establish an accepted rack condition, a rigid mounting point and an X / Y baseline. Compare later readings with that reference.</p><div class="ops-precision"><div><strong>±0.01°</strong><span>High-precision candidate</span></div><div><strong>±0.1°</strong><span>Standard-precision candidate</span></div></div><p class="ops-note">Select accuracy for the change you need to review. Set alarm thresholds separately with the rack specialist.</p><a class="ops-text-link" href="https://www.hitelecom.com/product/tilt-sensor">Explore tilt sensors <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
    <div class="ops-signal-header"><h3>Three behaviours. Three review paths.</h3><span>Signal illustrations · Not measured data</span></div>
    <div class="ops-signal-cards">
      <article><p class="ops-kicker">NORMAL LOADING REBOUND</p><svg viewBox="0 0 330 108" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative angle signal oscillates briefly and returns to the baseline"><path class="ops-chart-grid" d="M0 82H330M0 25H330"/><path class="ops-chart-base" d="M0 64H330"/><path class="ops-chart-signal" d="M0 64H55C66 64 65 20 76 24S85 94 95 86S106 42 115 45S129 78 139 74S150 56 162 59S176 68 188 66S218 64 245 64H330"/></svg><h4>Return to baseline</h4><p>Use the agreed return and duration conditions to avoid unnecessary escalation from normal handling.</p><div class="ops-signal-action">Review the operating context</div></article>
      <article><p class="ops-kicker">SUSTAINED ANGLE CHANGE</p><svg viewBox="0 0 330 108" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative angle signal changes and remains away from its initial baseline"><path class="ops-chart-grid" d="M0 82H330M0 25H330"/><path class="ops-chart-base" d="M0 70H330"/><path class="ops-chart-signal amber" d="M0 70H80C100 70 115 40 140 38S170 39 190 38H330"/></svg><h4>Residual change persists</h4><p>Identify the upright and arrange a site check. Confirm the cause and persistence through professional inspection.</p><div class="ops-signal-action">Inspect the point and surrounding bay</div></article>
      <article><p class="ops-kicker">ABNORMAL IMPACT</p><svg viewBox="0 0 330 108" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative short impact spike followed by a return to baseline"><path class="ops-chart-grid" d="M0 82H330M0 25H330"/><path class="ops-chart-base" d="M0 64H330"/><path class="ops-chart-signal orange" d="M0 64H105L114 62L120 9L125 98L131 42L139 74L147 59L160 65L175 64H330"/></svg><h4>An impact may still matter</h4><p>Where the supplied impact mode is validated, retain the event for review even if the angle returns.</p><div class="ops-signal-action">Retain and investigate the event</div></article>
    </div>
    <details class="ops-disclosure"><summary>How the two signal paths are evaluated <span>+</span></summary><div><p>A low-pass path follows the stable orientation; a high-pass path can support dynamic-event analysis. Filtering, duration and return conditions are evaluated together. Short impacts require suitable acquisition or wake-up hardware and firmware: a one-minute angle sample alone cannot establish impact capture. Signal processing does not diagnose structural damage.</p></div></details>
    <div class="ops-spec-strip"><div><strong>1<span> min</span></strong><p>Reference angle measurement</p></div><div><strong>4<span> hrs</span></strong><p>Reference routine reporting</p></div><div><strong>Event</strong><p>Reporting configured separately</p></div><div><strong>10<span> years*</span></strong><p>Reference battery operating life</p></div></div>
    <p class="ops-note">*H310-TS180C reference profile: 25°C, normal signal, 1-minute angle measurement and 4-hour routine reporting. Battery configuration, event activity, impact mode and site conditions affect life. Event delivery and end-to-end delay are validated for the project.</p>
  </div></section>

  <WarehouseOpsCloud/>

  <section class="ops-section" id="wh-applications" data-module="05" aria-labelledby="applications-title"><div class="ops-wrap">
    <div class="ops-heading"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">05 / YOUR STORAGE ENVIRONMENT</p><h2 id="applications-title">Different warehouses.<br/>Specific monitoring tasks.</h2></div><p>Keep rack tilt at the centre. Add the environmental or equipment measurements your goods and workplace actually need.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-scenes">{scenes.map(s=><article><figure><ResponsiveImage imageKey={s.image as any} alt={`${s.title}: warehouse application illustration`} sizes="(max-width:700px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width:1100px) 46vw, 610px"/><figcaption><span>{s.n} / APPLICATION</span><h3>{s.title}</h3><small>Application illustration</small></figcaption></figure><div class="ops-scene-copy"><p>{s.text}</p><span>{s.tag}</span></div></article>)}</div>
    <details class="ops-disclosure ops-support"><summary>Supporting sensors, selected for the actual risk <span>+</span></summary><div class="ops-support-grid"><article><h4>Stock conditions</h4><p>Temperature and humidity for cold rooms or moisture-sensitive goods; suitable probe placement and ranges.</p></article><article><h4>Water & utilities</h4><p>Water-presence sensing near vulnerable stock, condensate routes or pipe connections.</p></article><article><h4>Equipment condition</h4><p>Vibration and temperature on defined refrigeration, conveyor or fixed machinery points.</p></article><article><h4>People & EHS interfaces</h4><p>Gas-specific sensing and verified interfaces to approved fire, access or personnel-help systems, where included in the project.</p></article><p class="ops-note">Dedicated fire, gas and personnel-protection systems remain subject to their approved design. Tilt monitoring is not a personnel detector, automatic safety interlock or substitute for those systems.</p></div></details>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ops-section ops-pale" id="wh-hardware" data-module="06" aria-labelledby="hardware-title"><div class="ops-wrap">
    <div class="ops-heading"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">06 / INSTALLATION & COMMISSIONING</p><h2 id="hardware-title">Install by zone.<br/>Commission by point.</h2></div><p>Plan small work areas around warehouse operations. Agree the mounting and clearance, activate with NFC and verify the complete data path.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-install-layout"><figure class="ops-install-photo"><div class="ops-photo-crop" style={crops.rack}><ResponsiveImage imageKey="warehouse-field-board" alt="Supplied retouched field photograph showing a sensor installed on warehouse racking" sizes="1260px"/></div><figcaption>Supplied retouched field photograph · Rack installation point</figcaption></figure><div class="ops-install-content"><div class="ops-install-mini"><figure><div class="ops-photo-crop" style={crops.device}><ResponsiveImage imageKey="warehouse-field-board" alt="Supplied retouched field photograph of a Hitelecom sensor and its rack mounting" sizes="1260px"/></div></figure><div><span class="ops-kicker">APPROVED MOUNTING</span><h3>No new holes.<br/>No welding.</h3><p>Use an approved fixing method that preserves the rack structure and operating clearances.</p></div></div><ol class="ops-install-steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h4>Agree the work window</h4><p>Confirm local isolation, vehicle routes and access permits before installation.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h4>Fix, identify & activate</h4><p>Mount securely. Bind the device to its upright. Use NFC to activate and set the network.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h4>Record the baseline</h4><p>After rack acceptance, record axes, X / Y reference, location and installation photographs.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h4>Verify & hand over</h4><p>Check received data, event delivery, acknowledgement and communication-loss behaviour.</p></div></li></ol><p class="ops-note">Aim to keep unaffected zones operating. Required local shutdowns and access controls follow site procedures.</p></div></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ops-section" id="wh-evidence" data-module="07" aria-labelledby="evidence-title"><div class="ops-wrap">
    <div class="ops-heading"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">07 / OPERATING RECORDS & EHS</p><h2 id="evidence-title">A record the next<br/>shift can use.</h2></div><p>Keep the location, measurement, responsible person and inspection outcome together. Support the existing EHS record and maintenance workflow.</p></div>
    <div class="ops-evidence-grid"><div class="ops-record"><header><span>EXAMPLE / EVENT RECORD</span><b>Awaiting field assessment</b></header><h3>WH-A / R03 / B02 / U01</h3><p>Rack upright · X-axis change</p><dl><div><dt>Measurement context</dt><dd>Baseline, latest value & timestamp</dd></div><div><dt>Response ownership</dt><dd>Receiver, acknowledgement & substitute</dd></div><div><dt>Site assessment</dt><dd>Isolation, photographs & specialist findings</dd></div><div><dt>Return to use</dt><dd>Repair, reinspection & authorised approval</dd></div></dl><small>Record structure illustration. Platform and customer-system responsibilities are agreed per project.</small></div><div class="ops-evidence-copy"><h3>Evaluate practical value.<br/>Keep safety decisions intact.</h3><p>Compare the same points and workload during a representative site evaluation.</p><ul><li><span>01</span>Unnecessary review workload</li><li><span>02</span>Time to acknowledge an event</li><li><span>03</span>Time to reach the correct bay</li><li><span>04</span>Time a zone remains restricted</li></ul><p class="ops-note">Agree definitions and acceptance criteria first. Necessary inspections and restrictions take priority over improving a metric.</p></div></div>
    <details class="ops-disclosure ops-standards"><summary>Inspection responsibilities & regional references <span>+</span></summary><div><p>Keep risk-based checks, damage reporting and competent assessment. Apply the duties, manufacturer instructions and inspection arrangements relevant to your site.</p><div class="ops-standards-grid"><article><span>GREAT BRITAIN</span><h4>HSE HSG76</h4><p>Risk-based internal checks and expert inspection at intervals no longer than 12 months, under the guidance.</p><a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/pubns/priced/hsg76.pdf#page=115">Read HSE guidance ↗</a></article><article><span>EUROPE</span><h4>EN 15635</h4><p>Use, inspection and maintenance of steel storage equipment. National duties and site procedures determine applicability.</p><a href="https://knowledge.bsigroup.com/products/steel-static-storage-systems-application-and-maintenance-of-storage-equipment">View standard scope ↗</a></article><article><span>UNITED STATES</span><h4>OSHA 1910.176</h4><p>Safe material storage and clear aisles. The cited rule does not specify an annual rack inspection interval.</p><a href="https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.176">Read OSHA requirements ↗</a></article><article><span>AUSTRALIA</span><h4>AS 4084.2:2023</h4><p>WorkSafe Victoria guidance calls for frequent checks and annual competent-person inspection for selective pallet racking.</p><a href="https://www.worksafe.vic.gov.au/pallet-racking-operation-and-maintenance">Read WorkSafe guidance ↗</a></article></div><p class="ops-note">Guidance and standards are not interchangeable with law. These references do not require tilt sensors. Sensor alerts do not assign a SEMA damage category or authorise return to use.</p></div></details>
    <div class="ops-evaluation"><div><p class="ops-eyebrow">BEFORE A WIDER ROLLOUT</p><h3>Prove the measurement.<br/>Test the response.</h3></div><p>Validate normal handling, target angle changes, coverage at operating load and named-person acknowledgement. Use an independent test fixture for controlled angle or impact tests.</p><a class="ops-text-link" href="#enquiry">Plan a site evaluation <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <WarehouseOpsFaq/>
  <WarehouseEnquiry/>
</div>
<script>import '../scripts/warehouse-enquiry-v15.js';</script>
